### CEILING: SPDK vfio-user transport caps any IO at 128 KiB (32 x 4 KiB pages).
# >128 KiB returns NVMe Internal Error (sc=0x06); GPU kernel __builtin_trap()s on it.
# nvmf_tgt log:  vfio_user.c:717 nvme_cmd_map_prps: *ERROR*: Too many page entries
# Cause: include/spdk/nvmf_transport.h
#   SPDK_NVMF_MAX_SGL_ENTRIES = 16
#   NVMF_REQ_MAX_BUFFERS      = SPDK_NVMF_MAX_SGL_ENTRIES*2 + 1 = 33
#   NVMF_VFIO_USER_DEFAULT_MAX_IO_SIZE = (33-1) << 12 = 128 KiB
# Also: SPDK nvme_cmd_map_prps reads the PRP list as a flat contiguous array
# from prp2 (gpa_to_vva(prp2, nents*8)); it does NOT follow per-page PRP chain
# pointers. So 4 MiB needs BOTH a max-buffers bump AND chain-following (or a
# physically-contiguous flat list) on the SPDK side. GPU side (chaining) is done
# and verified non-regressing (4K single-page + 8K..128K multi-page-single-list).

######################################################################
# 64 MiB SUPPORT — BUILT & UNIT-VALIDATED (2026-06-11 PM), reboot-gated
######################################################################
# Goal: lift the GPU-initiated KV path from the 128 KiB SPDK ceiling to 64 MiB.
#
# Changes (all built; live target still the OLD binary until restart):
# 1. SPDK (mmgaggle/spdk@rados-nkv), lib/nvmf/vfio_user.c + include/spdk/nvmf_transport.h:
#    - nvme_cmd_map_prps(): rewritten to FOLLOW PRP CHAINS and COALESCE
#      physically-contiguous pages into one iov per run. A contiguous buffer
#      (GPU VRAM P2P region) of any size collapses to a single data iov.
#    - NVMF_VFIO_USER_MAX_IOVECS decoupled from NVMF_REQ_MAX_BUFFERS and raised
#      to 128 (holds the transient per-PRP-list-page MAP_R mappings while a
#      chained list is walked; ~32 for 64 MiB). NVMF_REQ_MAX_BUFFERS left at 33
#      (it is ABI-size-checked via struct spdk_nvmf_ctrlr; uint8_t iovcnt caps
#      data iovs at 255 anyway — coalescing keeps it ~2).
#    - NVMF_VFIO_USER_DEFAULT_MAX_IO_SIZE decoupled -> 64 MiB; IO_UNIT_SIZE 128 KiB.
#    - Unit test test_nvme_cmd_map_prps rewritten for coalescing + a 4 MiB
#      CHAINED-list case -> ret==2 (PRP1 + one coalesced data iov). 43/43 PASS.
#    - kvdev_rados already defaults max_value_len = 64 MiB (ADR-0002); osd_max_
#      object_size = 128 MiB. No backend change needed.
# 2. rocm-xio (mmgaggle@nvme-kv):
#    - nvme-ep PRP-list CHAINING (calculatePrps + host pool prpListPagesPerCmd)
#      so the GPU emits a spec-correct chained list for >512-page values.
#    - xio-common.hip per-page phys resolver: heap scratch table (was stack[1024]
#      = 4 MiB cap) so mode-0 host-buffer stores resolve up to 64 MiB.
#    Rebuilt in-guest; verified non-regressing 4 KiB..128 KiB e2e on the OLD target.
#
# REMAINING (needs reboot — restarting nvmf_tgt drops the guest's live vfio-user
# /dev/nvme0, so the VM must relaunch -> burns the one-shot GPU -> host reboot):
#   Post-reboot one-shot recipe (stage ALL before the single GPU VM launch):
#   1. boot grub index 1 (GPU->vfio); sudo modprobe vfio-pci; confirm /dev/vfio/27
#   2. vstart Ceph + `ceph osd pool create kvpool`
#   3. start the NEW nvmf_tgt (build/bin/nvmf_tgt, dated >= 2026-06-11 17:08) with
#      LD_LIBRARY_PATH=ceph/build/lib; `scripts/rados-nkv up ... --pool kvpool
#      --namespace gpukv` (uses 64 MiB kvdev default).
#   4. **HOST-SIDE PRE-CHECK before launching the GPU VM** (don't waste the shot):
#      drive a >128 KiB (e.g. 4 MiB and 64 MiB) KV store/retrieve from a host
#      KV client (kv_host_shim) against the new target; confirm no "Too many page
#      entries" and correct lengths. Only then launch the GPU VM.
#   5. launch GPU VM; in guest rebuild not needed (binary already carries chaining
#      + resolver fix from this session — but re-scp if the qcow2 was rebuilt).
#   6. GPU 64 MiB capture:
#      - HEADLINE: mode-8 retrieve into VRAM (contiguous => coalesces to 1 iov):
#        xio-tester -m 8 --pci-mmio-bridge nvme-ep --controller /dev/nvme0 \
#          --kv-op retrieve --key gpukey64m --value-size 67108864 \
#          --data-buffer-size 67108864 --read-io 20   (expect length 67108864)
#      - store-verify: mode-0 store up to 64 MiB now resolves per-page phys;
